{"chunk_id": "4596e39cde5b", "text": "This section recounts two intertwined threads of the Ramayana. First, the climactic duel between the monkey brothers Vali and Sugriva rages with brutal intensity as they hurl trees and stones and tear at each other. Unable to distinguish them, Rama waits until Hanuman marks Sugriva with a garland; Rama then shoots Vali through the heart, restoring Sugriva to the throne of Kishkindhya. The narrative then shifts to Lanka, where Sita is imprisoned in the Ashoka grove under the guard of grotesque Rakshasi wardens who threaten her. Refusing Ravana and declaring absolute loyalty to Rama, she prepares to waste away rather than betray her husband. A compassionate Rakshasi, Trijata, comforts her and recounts a prophetic dream foretelling Ravana\u2019s downfall and Rama\u2019s ultimate victory, rekindling Sita\u2019s hope.\nRama kills Vali during his duel with Sugriva; Sita suffers captivity in Ashoka grove while Trijata consoles her with a prophetic dream of Ravana\u2019s downfall.\nThemes: Vali's death, Sita's captivity, prophetic dream, loyalty to Rama, Ravana's impending downfall", "vector": [0.0038382571656256914, -0.02676278166472912, 0.009959819726645947, 0.007541006430983543, -0.015610492788255215, 0.024825019761919975, -0.0203261636197567, -0.008415031246840954, -0.025055384263396263, -0.024621758610010147, 0.008713148534297943, 0.016545496881008148, 0.01054250355809927, 0.007188686169683933, -0.005830220878124237, 0.00035147322341799736, 0.04406712204217911, -0.015800204128026962, 0.028998659923672676, -0.0194182600826025, -0.0030404552817344666, 0.002772827399894595, -0.01278515625745058, 0.004434491042047739, 0.0019360670121386647, 0.006595839746296406, 0.011470731347799301, -0.036343179643154144, 0.03940565511584282, -0.004549672827124596, -0.018388401716947556, -0.014865200035274029, -0.011463955976068974, -0.0055761439725756645, -0.014052153564989567, 0.0023747733794152737, 0.004448041785508394, 0.008767351508140564, -0.001